    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for the quick look. i noticed US Patent 7,889,001 mentions phase-change material modules for thermal stabilization... it's a bit close to what we're doing. do you think that one poses any actual threat to our application, or is it easy enough to distinguish from our micro-channel/ceramic approach?",
